### 2. `.gitignore`

Create a file named exactly **`.gitignore`** in your project's root directory (right next to `main.py`). Paste these lines inside to ensure your `.env` file and temporary files never get tracked or uploaded to GitHub:

```text
# Environment configuration file (Keep secret!)
.env

# Python compilation and cache files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/

# OS temporary files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temp audio files generated during TTS streams
*.mp3